  "description": "Janus chess, Werner Schoendorf's chess on a 10x8 board (1978). Each side adds two pawns and two januses, which move as a bishop or a knight, standing between each rook and knight; king and queen change places. Otherwise it is chess: the pawn's double step and capture in passing, promotion on the far rank to a queen, janus, rook, bishop or knight, and castling, which puts the king on the b- or i-file with the rook beside it on the inside.",
